details.image_prompt:
{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two shallow matte ceramic bowls placed on an aged, weathered oak wood tabletop, capturing a 3/4 overhead angle (40°) that reveals the entire contents of the bowls. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, with the second bowl slightly blurred behind it. Inside each bowl is a generous mound of tossed whole-wheat spaghetti, perfectly coated in a glossy, smooth, amber-colored peanut-lime dressing. Shredded rotisserie chicken breast fibers are evenly distributed throughout the pasta, alongside crisp, bright green and purple shredded cabbage slaw and thin half-moons of fresh English cucumber. The dressing provides a realistic sheen on the noodles, with small, scattered specks of red pepper flakes and minced garlic visible throughout. Shallow depth of field ensures the textures of the tender chicken and firm cabbage are clearly identifiable. To the side, a simple stainless steel fork rests casually on the wood surface near a few stray shredded cabbage bits and a single lime wedge. Natural, soft side lighting from a window on the left creates gentle shadows, highlighting the vibrant colors and moisture of the ingredients. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small sauce drip on the bowl rim, slightly uneven ingredient distribution. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few tiny crumbs on the surface, a stray piece of cucumber on the table. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting, not cold or clinical. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
}
